"fullName": "Lambotte O", "lastName": "Lambotte", "firstName": "Olivier", "initials": "O", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4425-8516"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "APHP Médecine Interne/Immunologie Clinique, Hôpital Bicêtre, Paris, France."}, {"affiliation": "Université Paris-Saclay, INSERM U1184, CEA, Immunology of Viral Infections and Autoimmune Diseases, IDMIT Department, IBFJ, Fontenay-aux-Roses and Le Kremlin-Bicêtre, Paris, France."}]}}, {"fullName": "Mariette X", "lastName": "Mariette", "firstName": "Xavier", "initials": "X", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Université Paris-Saclay, INSERM, CEA, Centre de recherche en Immunologie des infections virales et des maladies auto-immunes; AP-HP. Université Paris-Saclay, Hôpital Bicêtre, Rheumatology Department, Le Kremlin Bicêtre, Paris, France."}]}}, {"fullName": "Prat A", "lastName": "Prat", "firstName": "Aleix", "initials": "A", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Translational Genomic and Targeted Therapeutics in Solid Tumors, Institut d'Investigacions Biomèdiques August Pi i Sunyer (IDIBAPS), Barcelona, Spain."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Medical Oncology, Hospital Clínic of Barcelona, Barcelona, Spain."}]}}, {"fullName": "Suárez-Almazor ME", "lastName": "Suárez-Almazor", "firstName": "Maria E", "initials": "ME", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Section of Rheumatology/Clinical Immunology, The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center, Houston, TX, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-5709-6734"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4425-8516"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "6", "journalIssueId": 2953186, "dateOfPublication": "2020 May", "monthOfPublication": 5, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nat Rev Dis Primers", "title": "Nature reviews. Disease primers", "essn": "2056-676X", "issn": "2056-676X", "nlmid": "101672103", "isoabbreviation": "Nat Rev Dis Primers"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-05-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "38", "abstractText": "Cancer immunotherapies have changed the landscape of cancer treatment during the past few decades. Among them, immune checkpoint inhibitors, which target PD-1, PD-L1 and CTLA-4, are increasingly used for certain cancers; however, this increased use has resulted in increased reports of immune-related adverse events (irAEs). These irAEs are unique and are different to those of traditional cancer therapies, and typically have a delayed onset and prolonged duration. IrAEs can involve any organ or system. These effects are frequently low grade and are treatable and reversible; however, some adverse effects can be severe and lead to permanent disorders. Management is primarily based on corticosteroids and other immunomodulatory agents, which should be prescribed carefully to reduce the potential of short-term and long-term complications. Thoughtful management of irAEs is important in optimizing quality of life and long-term outcomes.", "affiliation": "Department of Autoimmune Diseases, ICMiD, Barcelona, Spain. mramos@clinic.cat.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P30 CA008748", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P30 CA016672", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Immunologic Factors", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TU", "qualifierName": "therapeutic use"}]